You're probably right, there would probably be not many people who
would want to move files from a patched game to an unpatched one.
The flags wouldn't be a problem, but as you pointed out, monsters and
items WOULD be problem in bidirectional compatibility.

And changing the current comparison that requires equal numbers for
objects, monsters and artifacts to one that allows loading files with
these numbers smaller than the game loading the file, probably isn't safe.
Because we can't expect every new item or monster to be added to the end
of the list, because many conditions in the game require some kind of
grouping of monsters and items that behave similarly in some situation.

But the flags don't NEED to be in any specific order, new ones can safely
be added at the end of the flag struct. So I think placeholders for
additional flags would still be a good idea.

